course: dictionary
lesson: 2485
title: A helper in church
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A deacon is a helper in a church. In some churches a deacon is a minister who ranks below a priest. In many Protestant churches, a deacon is a member chosen to help with services, care and practical work. Context gives you the clue: «Deacons, elders, church wardens and many volunteers care for people, buildings and money.» The sentence puts deacons with other church helpers, so a deacon is one of the people who serve the church.
explain: Read the words around the word. In church lessons, the deacon reads the Gospel, helps at communion and visits the sick. Those jobs all show care and service. If you swap in «helper» for «deacon», the sentence still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Sometimes a word appears as a name. «The Byzantine writer Leo the Deacon described Prince Sviatoslav...» Here deacon is part of a man's name, not a job he does every day. The clue is that the name is about a church role, and the rest of the sentence tells you about the prince and his wars. You do not need every detail to get the main idea.
fact: A deacon is a church helper, or a minister below a priest in some churches.
fact: In the Bible, the first deacons were chosen to help share food fairly.
fact: A deacon may read the Gospel, help at communion and visit the sick.
fact: «Deacon» is a church word, so the words around it, like church, service and prayer, give you clues.
fact: You can check a meaning by swapping in a simpler word, such as helper, and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Deacons, elders, church wardens and many volunteers care for people, buildings and money.» What do deacons do in a church? | Bake cakes for the school fair | *Help with services and look after people | Own all the church land | Ring the church bells only
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence that means people who give their time to help. | prayer | buildings | *volunteers | money
exercise: «Leo the Deacon described Prince Sviatoslav.» What does deacon in his name suggest? | A kind of bread | *A church helper or minister | A prince who ruled a country | A horseman of the steppe
test: In the Bible, the first deacons were chosen for what job? | Writing history books | Leading armies into war | *Sharing food fairly | Building temples alone
test: Which person is most like a deacon, a church helper? | A prince fighting a war | Pechenegs, horsemen of the steppe | *A church warden | A Greek-speaking emperor
exam: Using the clues, what does deacon most likely mean in «The deacon read the Gospel at the service»? | A kind of sweet bread | *A church minister or helper who reads and serves | A river in Russia | A soldier from the steppe
